  "content": {
    "title": "Coachella 2022: Karol G surprises fans with J Balvin, debuts new single 'Provenza'",
    "text": "April 24, 2022Updated April 25, 2022, 9:52 a.m. PTKarol G commanded the Coachella Stage once more during Weekend 2 of the festival, delighting her passionate fans — many of whom had donned vibrant blue hair like the singer — with a string of surprises.From the moment the Colombian star opened with \"El Makinon,\" the festival grounds turned into a huge dance floor, the audience moving and even twirling one another. \"We Latinos do it like this!\" Karol G teased before belting out \"De Mi Ya Te Olvidaste.\"At every turn, there was a surprise: A cover of DJ Tiesto's EDM anthem \"Don't Be Shy\"; a costume change from a sparkly white, one-piece ensemble to a jumpsuit in yellow, blue and red like the Colombian flag; and special guests Becky G and J Balvin.\"She is the sweetest thing there is and it's an honor to have her here,\" Karol G told the audience as Becky G made her way onto the stage. Though the crowd may have anticipated Becky G's appearance — she had also joined Karol G on Weekend 1— they greeted her enthusiastically and sang along to the duo's hit song, \"Mamiii.\" Fans were also waiting for the return of a spectacular medley of songs by all-Latino artists that Karol G had whipped up Weekend 1. To say it was iconic is an understatement.It included:Carlos Santana's \"La Bamba\"Gloria Estefan's \"Conga\"Selena's \"Como la Flor\"Ricky Martin's \"María\"Los Del Rio's \"La Macarena\"Celia Cruz's \"La Vida es un Carnaval\"Daddy Yankee's \"Gasolina\"Shakira's \"Hips Don't Lie\"Luis Fonsi and Daddy Yankee's \"Despacito\"It ended with J Balvin's \"Mi Gente,\" at which point the Prince of Reggaeton himself appeared onstage to sing along with Karol G, causing a roar from the crowd and everyone to immediately pull out their phones to capture the moment. Karol G recently dominated the Latin American Music Awards, taking home six (the most awards of the night). But she wasn't resting on her laurels. Her Weekend 2 concertogers also saw the first public performance of her new single, \"Provenza.\"\"I kept this song to perform on this stage!\" she declared.Eliana Perez covers the eastern Coachella Valley. Reach her at eliana.perez@desertsun.com or on Twitter @ElianaPress.",
